   "line": 7,
   "text": "Take the smallest burst, seventeen hundred and eighteen hundred hertz together. When their dots line up, the sum swells. The faster dot gains four and a half degrees per sample. Through the notch, eighteen hundred is set back eleven point six degrees more, and must catch that up first. [surprise-oh] The swell is two point five eight samples late.",
