  {
   "line": 9,
   "text": "So add a filter that only delays. A pole inside the circle, radius point six five, at twelve hundred hertz. A zero on the same line, outside, at one over point six five. From any tone, the zero is always one point five four times as far as the pole. That ratio never changes, so compared with zero hertz, every tone passes a hundred percent. That's an all-pass.",
