  {
   "line": 11,
   "text": "Why not speed the late tones up? Running the all-pass backwards puts a pole outside the circle, and every echo grows. You can't play a tone before it arrives. You can only make everyone else wait. [sigh] Next ticket. Three notches, multiplied into one rule. Perfect on the laptop. On a cheap eight-bit chip, it hums, louder and louder.",
